# libksba -- X.509, CMS and OCSP parsing for gnupg.
#
# Needed by gnupg, which is needed by gpgme, which flatpak takes as a hard
# dependency with no option guard. Nothing else in Duct wants X.509 parsing.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://gnupg.org/ftp/gcrypt/libksba/libksba-1.6.7.tar.bz2
SRC_SHA256=cf72510b8ebb4eb6693eef765749d83677a03c79291a311040a5bfd79baab763
SRC_DIR=libksba-1.6.7

# --disable-doc, off to save build time rather than because it would fail:
# texinfo is packaged and the documentation would build.
#
# --disable-static RESTATES A DEFAULT and is kept for consistency with every
# other library recipe here; configure reports "[default=no]" for static, so
# libtool already builds shared only. The default belongs to libtool rather than
# to this package.
#
# NOT PASSED: --enable-valgrind-tests, which is off by default and would need
# valgrind, which is not packaged. Named because a self-test option that quietly
# needs a tool nobody has is exactly the kind of thing switched on hopefully
# during a later debugging session.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static --disable-doc"
